From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Subject: arm64: dts: odroid-go-ultra: set DSI clocks to match the panel mode

The DSI node added by 0002 pins GP0 and the DSI bit clock to 344976000
(28.748 MHz x 12), but the panel mode uses a 29170 kHz pixel clock
(350.04 MHz bit clock for RGB888 on 2 lanes).

The meson DSI driver does request 350.04 MHz, but at that point the
pixel clock is still prepared and vclk2_div is CLK_SET_RATE_GATE, so
GP0 is rate-protected and the request is silently rounded to the old
rate. The panel then runs at 58.88 Hz instead of 60 Hz.

Override the assigned rates so the clocks match the mode. Measured
refresh rate after this change: 59.91 Hz.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts	2026-10-10 23:05:12.442149479 +0900
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts	2026-10-10 23:05:12.444861577 +0900
@@ -826,3 +826,8 @@
 		remote-endpoint = <&mipi_in_panel>;
 	};
 };
+
+/* Lakka: run the DSI clocks at the rate the panel mode asks for */
+&mipi_dsi {
+	assigned-clock-rates = <350040000>, <0>, <350040000>, <0>, <0>;
+};
